        [
          "🧠 1. Core Concept"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20924eb1-ed54-80d2-8d80-eb18c5065cff",
      "type": "text",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Exception handling in Spring Boot",
          [
            [
              "b"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " allows developers to gracefully handle errors and unexpected situations during runtime. Instead of showing raw error messages or stack traces to users, we can return clean, customized responses—like proper error codes and messages. Tools like "
        ],
        [
          "@ControllerAdvice",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " and "
        ],
        [
          "@ExceptionHandler",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " make this process centralized and reusable across the application."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20924eb1-ed54-80af-b0b3-e8d1d7928af7",
      "type": "divider"
    },
    {
      "id": "20924eb1-ed54-8099-8a79-f514721b827e",
      "type": "sub_header",
      "richText": [
        [
          "🎯 2. Key Interview Points"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20924eb1-ed54-808b-a2e2-def452a117ca",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "🔹 "
        ],
        [
          "What is ",
          [
            [
              "b"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          "@ExceptionHandler",
          [
            [
              "b"
            ],
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " and how does it work?",
          [
            [
              "b"
            ]
          ]
        ]
      ],
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "20924eb1-ed54-806b-8cf5-ceebc7c1ec32",
          "type": "text",
          "richText": [
            [
              "It maps specific exceptions to custom handler methods in your controller classes."
            ]
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20924eb1-ed54-80d3-b52c-d6b98aa0c2d8",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "🔹 "
        ],
        [
          "What is ",
          [
            [
              "b"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          "@ControllerAdvice",
          [
            [
              "b"
            ],
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          "?",
          [
            [
              "b"
            ]
          ]
        ]
      ],
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "20924eb1-ed54-809e-a7d9-e7db1b3c6428",
          "type": "text",
          "richText": [
            [
              "It’s a global error-handling component that can catch exceptions from "
            ],
            [
              "any",
              [
                [
                  "i"
                ]
              ]
            ],
            [
              " controller class."
            ]
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20924eb1-ed54-8098-b749-f4f98cb4e713",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "🔹 "
        ],
        [
          "How do you return custom error responses (e.g., JSON) for exceptions?",
          [
            [
              "b"
            ]
          ]
        ]
      ],
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "20924eb1-ed54-80f9-a098-ee5f46af0217",
          "type": "text",
          "richText": [
            [
              "By using "
            ],
            [
              "@ResponseBody",
              [
                [
                  "c"
                ]
              ]
            ],
            [
              " or returning a "
            ],
            [
              "ResponseEntity",
              [
                [
                  "c"
                ]
              ]
            ],
            [
              " with status and body."
            ]
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20924eb1-ed54-8053-be56-d8864734e335",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "🔹 "
        ],
        [
          "Why centralize exception handling?",
          [
            [
              "b"
            ]
          ]
        ]
      ],
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "20924eb1-ed54-80f9-bbd1-d81d3256a98e",
          "type": "text",
          "richText": [
            [
              "Promotes cleaner code, consistency, and easier maintenance across multiple controllers."
            ]
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
